1
00:00:39,500 --> 00:00:42,840
Something will work out, I'm sure.

2
00:00:55,880 --> 00:00:59,880
Anyone without a job, come to me.

3
00:00:59,880 --> 00:01:04,480
Not that I have one either, so don't worry.

4
00:01:04,480 --> 00:01:18,240
Look, even the burning
steel will be fine eventually.

5
00:01:20,360 --> 00:01:27,440
You get it, right? Got it, got it.
Once you do, shut up and follow me.

6
00:01:40,920 --> 00:01:42,900
Atami Octopus Trip

7
00:01:47,160 --> 00:01:48,620
Atami, you say?

8
00:01:49,560 --> 00:01:52,500
Yep, Atami. I've already booked a hotel too.

9
00:01:53,160 --> 00:01:54,880
A fancy hotel, is it?

10
00:01:55,760 --> 00:01:58,560
It's quite a famous hotel.

11
00:01:58,560 --> 00:02:01,060
The octopus dishes there are really delicious,
you know.

12
00:02:01,060 --> 00:02:03,640
Yeah, that's what sealed the deal.

13
00:02:04,480 --> 00:02:05,705
Wait a minute.

14
00:02:05,755 --> 00:02:09,300
Normally, the organizer decides
where the company trip goes, right?

15
00:02:09,760 --> 00:02:12,440
Why are you deciding without consulting me?

16
00:02:12,740 --> 00:02:14,117
If I let you decide,

17
00:02:14,167 --> 00:02:16,880
I have no idea where you'll take us.

18
00:02:17,200 --> 00:02:19,075
Last time, you embezzled the travel money

19
00:02:19,125 --> 00:02:21,400
and tried to cover it up
with sightseeing around Tokyo.

20
00:02:21,820 --> 00:02:26,140
You even dragged us off to some
mountain in the middle of nowhere.

21
00:02:26,860 --> 00:02:30,080
Leaving things to Ryo-chan
never turns out well.

22
00:02:30,800 --> 00:02:33,620
So what am I supposed to do,
as the organizer?

23
00:02:34,480 --> 00:02:37,140
If the destination's already decided,
there's nothing for me to do.

24
00:02:37,140 --> 00:02:39,280
There's plenty to do.

25
00:02:39,900 --> 00:02:41,680
Arranging transportation.

26
00:02:41,680 --> 00:02:43,360
Checking attendance.

27
00:02:43,360 --> 00:02:44,820
Printing on the day.

28
00:02:44,820 --> 00:02:48,260
And collecting the travel money.

29
00:02:48,260 --> 00:02:51,440
I'll cover my share and the chief's.

30
00:02:51,440 --> 00:02:52,120
Got it?

31
00:02:52,120 --> 00:02:54,700
Whatever you do, don't embezzle anything.

32
00:02:54,700 --> 00:02:56,720
Yeah, yeah, understood.

33
00:02:58,000 --> 00:03:00,040
Well, I'm off to the station.

34
00:03:00,040 --> 00:03:01,340
Good work.

35
00:03:02,460 --> 00:03:03,600
Octopus cuisine

36
00:03:04,480 --> 00:03:10,280
Can't wait! I've eaten there once,
and their octopus dishes are exquisite.

37
00:03:10,700 --> 00:03:16,540
Hmph, all this over just octopus. Don't go absentmindedly embezzling,
Ryo-chan.

38
00:03:16,540 --> 00:03:20,260
Why don't you write something on the envelope?
Yeah, yeah.

39
00:03:20,900 --> 00:03:22,780
Oc-to-tto!

40
00:03:25,260 --> 00:03:29,100
Bobby and the others are going on a trip?

41
00:03:29,100 --> 00:03:31,880
Yeah, the whole station is going to Atami.

42
00:03:31,880 --> 00:03:34,720
What a shame,
when you've come all the way to Japan.

43
00:03:34,720 --> 00:03:38,140
It's a stupid trip just to go eat octopus.

44
00:03:38,920 --> 00:03:43,800
Since I was made organizer from the start,
I reluctantly collected the fees, at least.

45
00:03:44,460 --> 00:03:47,520
Honestly,
what's so special about this trip anyway?

46
00:03:50,120 --> 00:03:52,200
Senpai, you're drinking too much.

47
00:03:52,680 --> 00:03:58,320
Shut up! Why do we have to go all
the way to Atami just to eat octopus?

48
00:04:00,660 --> 00:04:02,460
It's the Octopus Hall!

49
00:04:02,920 --> 00:04:04,820
Ugh... I can't breathe...

50
00:04:04,820 --> 00:04:06,520
Ryo-san's really raging, isn't he?

51
00:04:07,000 --> 00:04:09,660
Yeah, the fact that they chose
the destination without him

52
00:04:09,660 --> 00:04:11,520
seems to have really ticked him off.

53
00:04:11,520 --> 00:04:14,720
Ryo-san, let's get drinking tonight!

54
00:04:14,940 --> 00:04:16,340
I'll keep drinking with you until morning!

55
00:04:16,620 --> 00:04:17,740
I see!

56
00:04:18,320 --> 00:04:20,260
Alright, let's drink to that octopus!

57
00:04:20,880 --> 00:04:22,160
Yeah!

58
00:04:22,540 --> 00:04:24,560
Screw the octopus!

59
00:04:24,560 --> 00:04:24,760
Argh!

60
00:04:25,760 --> 00:04:27,820
Yeah, yeah, yeah!

61
00:04:28,260 --> 00:04:32,020
Cheers, cheers, it's about that time.

62
00:04:32,020 --> 00:04:33,860
Could we get the check, please?

63
00:04:33,860 --> 00:04:34,620
Hey,

64
00:04:34,620 --> 00:04:36,480
Do you have any money?

65
00:04:36,480 --> 00:04:37,480
Money

66
00:04:38,660 --> 00:04:40,700
Where did it go?

67
00:04:45,440 --> 00:04:48,060
There's this much here, isn't there?

68
00:04:49,340 --> 00:04:50,860
Octopus.

69
00:04:50,860 --> 00:04:52,760
Speaking of octopus,

70
00:04:54,560 --> 00:05:01,460
Eeeeeh! That's the prize money from when
I won the kite-flying contest last month.

71
00:05:02,420 --> 00:05:06,980
Whoa! Honda-san, the barber's a killer!

72
00:05:07,460 --> 00:05:08,140
While drinking,

73
00:05:08,140 --> 00:05:09,180
Aaaaah!

74
00:05:12,460 --> 00:05:19,680
Bring all the sake you've got!
Ryo-san's getting a little tipsy, aru!

75
00:05:24,200 --> 00:05:24,580
Thanks for everything.

76
00:05:25,840 --> 00:05:28,040
Whew, the morning sun is dazzling!

77
00:05:28,040 --> 00:05:29,860
What a refreshing morning.

78
00:05:29,860 --> 00:05:32,000
We really drank all night

79
00:05:32,460 --> 00:05:34,360
Ryotsu, what happened to the bill?

80
00:05:35,980 --> 00:05:37,055
Well, by luck,

81
00:05:37,105 --> 00:05:40,000
I had the prize money from
the kite-flying contest.

82
00:05:41,400 --> 00:05:45,180
Didn't we also drink the night
of the kite-flying contest?

83
00:05:45,180 --> 00:05:47,960
Right, we drank with Ryotsu's prize money.

84
00:05:47,960 --> 00:05:50,400
When we ran short,
we all chipped in, didn't we?

85
00:05:51,800 --> 00:05:53,300
Then where's this money?

86
00:05:53,980 --> 00:05:57,196
Ryo-chan,
so you don't accidentally blow it all,

87
00:05:57,246 --> 00:05:58,880
write something on the envelope.

88
00:05:59,540 --> 00:06:02,600
Yeah, yeah. Got it.

89
00:06:03,540 --> 00:06:06,000
That was the money for the company trip!

90
00:06:06,480 --> 00:06:09,380
You spent the trip money?

91
00:06:09,900 --> 00:06:11,580
W-what are we gonna do, Ryotsu?

92
00:06:22,100 --> 00:06:24,100
At last, it's here, Ohara.

93
00:06:24,100 --> 00:06:25,900
Indeed it is, President.

94
00:06:25,900 --> 00:06:28,620
So they serve this kind of dish!

95
00:06:29,040 --> 00:06:31,500
They say they only use
freshly caught octopus.

96
00:06:31,500 --> 00:06:33,200
I'm really looking forward to it.

97
00:06:33,200 --> 00:06:35,880
But why are we meeting at the wharf?

98
00:06:35,880 --> 00:06:37,220
Are we going by boat, I wonder?

99
00:06:37,220 --> 00:06:40,000
Though I don't see a boat.

100
00:06:40,740 --> 00:06:42,880
It's about time to leave, isn't it?

101
00:06:48,000 --> 00:06:49,040
Th-this is...

102
00:06:50,440 --> 00:06:51,860
A-a submarine?

103
00:06:52,380 --> 00:06:53,840
Look, over there.

104
00:06:55,180 --> 00:06:57,580
Katsushika Station party?

105
00:06:58,520 --> 00:06:59,920
N-no way...

106
00:06:59,920 --> 00:07:03,380
Yeah, everyone, sorry to keep you waiting!

107
00:07:04,560 --> 00:07:06,960
Ryotsu, what is the meaning of this?

108
00:07:06,960 --> 00:07:08,480
You're not seriously
going to travel in that?

109
00:07:10,080 --> 00:07:12,360
The main event of this
trip is the octopus cuisine.

110
00:07:12,360 --> 00:07:15,540
So I thought I'd let everyone experience
what it's like to be an octopus.

111
00:07:15,540 --> 00:07:17,380
I've prepared a submarine.

112
00:07:18,420 --> 00:07:20,660
What do you think? Good idea, right?

113
00:07:25,860 --> 00:07:27,200
Sorry about this, Jodie.

114
00:07:27,200 --> 00:07:28,880
for asking so much of you.

115
00:07:29,820 --> 00:07:31,940
If it means I get to travel with Bobby,

116
00:07:31,940 --> 00:07:34,100
I'm more than happy to help out.

117
00:07:35,180 --> 00:07:37,080
Alright, once everyone's aboard,

118
00:07:37,080 --> 00:07:41,020
Yes, then, all aboard, we're off!

119
00:07:52,620 --> 00:07:57,600
Come on, everyone, let loose and have fun!
Easier said than done, though.

120
00:07:58,620 --> 00:08:04,240
It's too quiet, I can't settle down. Not being
able to see the view outside is just not right.

121
00:08:04,880 --> 00:08:06,140
Right, that's right.

122
00:08:06,140 --> 00:08:07,580
Click! There we go.

123
00:08:08,780 --> 00:08:11,020
This is the footage
from the external camera.

124
00:08:15,400 --> 00:08:16,960
What a monotonous scene.

125
00:08:18,800 --> 00:08:21,560
Just watching it is depressing.

126
00:08:21,560 --> 00:08:22,500
Ryotsu!

127
00:08:22,960 --> 00:08:24,540
I have a simple question, though.

128
00:08:24,540 --> 00:08:26,880
About renting a submarine like this...

129
00:08:26,880 --> 00:08:28,880
How much does it cost?

130
00:08:29,940 --> 00:08:30,340
Oh yeah.

131
00:08:30,340 --> 00:08:32,920
We've also got karaoke set up.

132
00:08:34,240 --> 00:08:34,840
Let's do it!

133
00:08:35,440 --> 00:08:36,900
Hey, Erifōzu!

134
00:08:38,200 --> 00:08:41,440
Then I'll have the honor of singing first.

135
00:08:42,880 --> 00:08:46,180
For the bad guys, a Robo-deka punch!

136
00:08:46,180 --> 00:08:51,520
Blast them off to the end of the gears!

137
00:08:52,720 --> 00:08:53,620
Robo!

138
00:08:53,720 --> 00:08:57,420
For the clever ones, a Robo-deka kick!

139
00:08:57,420 --> 00:09:00,860
Holding the... bringing everyone's joy.

140
00:09:00,860 --> 00:09:02,500
Let's really vanish.

141
00:09:05,320 --> 00:09:08,540
Ban-ban-ban-ban-ban-ban-ban-chū!

142
00:09:11,820 --> 00:09:14,800
I've come along with you too.

143
00:09:15,440 --> 00:09:18,960
This is Robo-Digan-Banchū!

144
00:09:30,100 --> 00:09:31,660
Alright, we've arrived.

145
00:09:32,600 --> 00:09:35,360
It's Atami.

146
00:09:35,360 --> 00:09:38,340
But we're pretty far from the shore,
aren't we?

147
00:09:38,340 --> 00:09:41,420
Apparently the water here is
too shallow to get any closer.

148
00:09:41,920 --> 00:09:43,920
So how are we supposed to get to the hotel?

149
00:09:44,480 --> 00:09:45,900
Don't worry.

150
00:09:46,500 --> 00:09:47,260
That's it.

151
00:09:57,420 --> 00:09:58,840
We're going by rubber boat?

152
00:09:58,840 --> 00:09:59,660
Yes.

153
00:10:02,840 --> 00:10:05,720
Come on, everyone, row, row!

154
00:10:07,660 --> 00:10:11,640
Don't tell me we came all the way to
Atami just to be made to row a boat!

155
00:10:11,640 --> 00:10:14,480
It's like the Normandy landing!

156
00:10:14,480 --> 00:10:16,580
It's all Ryotsu's fault.

157
00:10:17,700 --> 00:10:19,780
So this is the wonderful hotel.

158
00:10:21,320 --> 00:10:22,720
How wonderful this is.

159
00:10:23,600 --> 00:10:25,200
Wow, how beautiful!

160
00:10:25,200 --> 00:10:26,560
How lovely.

161
00:10:27,520 --> 00:10:30,100
Ryotsu, hurry up and show us to our rooms.

162
00:10:30,100 --> 00:10:33,380
I'm already worn out from rowing that boat.

163
00:10:33,960 --> 00:10:34,740
Ryotsu!

164
00:10:35,440 --> 00:10:37,100
Everything's ready.

165
00:10:37,100 --> 00:10:38,460
I see.

166
00:10:38,460 --> 00:10:41,320
Now, everyone, let me show you to the hotel.

167
00:10:41,940 --> 00:10:43,940
Right this way, please.

168
00:10:45,020 --> 00:10:46,700
Wow, this is luxurious.

169
00:10:54,800 --> 00:10:56,680
We're walking quite a bit, aren't we?

170
00:10:57,420 --> 00:10:58,520
Oh-chan, are we there yet?

171
00:10:59,800 --> 00:11:01,020
Almost there.

172
00:11:01,780 --> 00:11:03,200
Is that where we're coming out?

173
00:11:03,360 --> 00:11:05,660
We're staying at the annex.

174
00:11:05,660 --> 00:11:06,760
The annex?

175
00:11:09,240 --> 00:11:10,880
We've arrived, here it is.

176
00:11:14,380 --> 00:11:17,000
A wonderful hotel, the annex.

177
00:11:17,000 --> 00:11:20,400
That's completely different from the main building behind us,
isn't it?

178
00:11:20,400 --> 00:11:23,060
That's why I said it was the annex,
didn't I?

179
00:11:24,660 --> 00:11:26,940
You expect us to stay in a place like this?

180
00:11:26,940 --> 00:11:32,360
I protested fiercely to the hotel,
but they wouldn't accept it at all.

181
00:11:32,360 --> 00:11:34,500
What's going on, Lord Ryo?

182
00:11:34,500 --> 00:11:43,020
Apparently, in recent years there have been more cases of group
guests causing an uproar inside the hotel and disturbing other guests.

183
00:11:43,020 --> 00:11:50,940
To prevent that kind of situation, they say all group
guests have been asked to stay here starting this year.

184
00:11:50,940 --> 00:11:52,400
No way.

185
00:11:52,860 --> 00:11:55,260
How do you come up with such lies?

186
00:11:55,700 --> 00:11:57,060
They can hear you, you know.

187
00:12:01,100 --> 00:12:02,180
What is this?

188
00:12:02,180 --> 00:12:03,660
What a filthy room.

189
00:12:04,460 --> 00:12:08,960
I never thought we'd come to eat octopus
and end up sleeping in an octopus room.

190
00:12:11,460 --> 00:12:13,840
Good grief, this is the worst room ever.

191
00:12:14,360 --> 00:12:17,120
Ryo-san,
we're at least getting proper meals, right?

192
00:12:17,560 --> 00:12:20,840
We came here looking forward to octopus dishes,
you know.

193
00:12:20,840 --> 00:12:23,580
Of course. I'm getting them now.

194
00:12:23,580 --> 00:12:24,560
Getting them?

195
00:12:25,060 --> 00:12:27,260
No, no, I mean cooking. Cooking!

196
00:12:27,260 --> 00:12:29,680
They should be cooking them right now.

197
00:12:29,680 --> 00:12:32,420
The hotel's top-class chefs are

198
00:12:39,080 --> 00:12:40,080
We're not catching any, are we?

199
00:12:40,080 --> 00:12:42,960
We have to, no matter what,
before dinnertime

200
00:12:42,960 --> 00:12:45,740
get enough octopus.

201
00:13:10,940 --> 00:13:15,660
We've come all the way to Atami, so
let's take a hot spring bath before dinner.

202
00:13:15,660 --> 00:13:18,120
Good idea, let's all go together.

203
00:13:18,720 --> 00:13:21,120
Ryotsu, there's a bath, right?

204
00:13:21,120 --> 00:13:22,420
Of course there is.

205
00:13:22,420 --> 00:13:25,980
The bathhouse is here.

206
00:13:26,980 --> 00:13:27,380
What is this?

207
00:13:31,900 --> 00:13:35,260
Guests in the annex are apparently
supposed to use this one.

208
00:13:35,760 --> 00:13:40,320
As I mentioned earlier,
group guests often cause trouble,

209
00:13:40,800 --> 00:13:41,280
What's that supposed to mean?!

210
00:13:42,460 --> 00:13:43,820
You've got to be kidding!

211
00:13:44,040 --> 00:13:46,460
We paid good money to stay here!

212
00:13:46,640 --> 00:13:49,320
Why should we have to stay
in some place like that?!

213
00:13:49,960 --> 00:13:53,400
No, I mean,
this is the hotel's policy, so...

214
00:13:53,880 --> 00:13:55,940
I can't accept a policy like that!

215
00:13:56,460 --> 00:13:58,780
We should file a strong protest about this.

216
00:13:58,780 --> 00:14:00,120
You're right, Chief.

217
00:14:00,120 --> 00:14:00,700
Yeah.

218
00:14:01,380 --> 00:14:02,060
Uh-oh.

219
00:14:02,060 --> 00:14:03,900
Let's all go to the front desk together.

220
00:14:03,900 --> 00:14:07,000
That's right, that's right!

221
00:14:07,000 --> 00:14:10,960
Didn't they say we could use the main building's bath,
at least?

222
00:14:10,960 --> 00:14:13,000
Well, I'll show you the way.

223
00:14:20,040 --> 00:14:21,660
There are this many people here, so

224
00:14:21,660 --> 00:14:24,500
if we act confident, no one should notice.

225
00:14:25,440 --> 00:14:27,740
Come on, everyone, this way.

226
00:14:28,580 --> 00:14:30,440
Please, come right in.

227
00:14:31,820 --> 00:14:35,000
An outdoor bath!

228
00:14:37,060 --> 00:14:38,960
Now that's what I call refined.

229
00:14:45,440 --> 00:14:48,220
Ryo-san, that's a woman over there!

230
00:14:49,360 --> 00:14:50,720
Is this mixed bathing?

231
00:14:52,280 --> 00:14:54,220
It happens sometimes.

232
00:14:54,220 --> 00:14:56,460
Only the entrances are
separated by gender like this.

233
00:14:56,460 --> 00:14:58,660
The hot spring connected inside...

234
00:14:59,280 --> 00:15:01,200
What should we do, Chief?

235
00:15:01,200 --> 00:15:02,680
Ohara-kun.

236
00:15:03,200 --> 00:15:05,800
There's no need to be embarrassed.

237
00:15:07,000 --> 00:15:09,380
It goes both ways, so just act confident.

238
00:15:09,380 --> 00:15:10,080
Hey.

239
00:15:13,060 --> 00:15:14,340
Excuse us, excuse us.

240
00:15:14,340 --> 00:15:16,600
Pardon us, miss.

241
00:15:19,320 --> 00:15:19,720
What?

242
00:15:24,080 --> 00:15:26,060
You're Bookshelf Old Man, aren't you?

243
00:15:26,060 --> 00:15:27,660
Well, if it isn't Ryo-chan.

244
00:15:27,660 --> 00:15:28,760
Long time no see.

245
00:15:28,760 --> 00:15:30,920
What are you doing in a place like this?

246
00:15:30,920 --> 00:15:34,780
We've been staying here for a week for
a training camp from Bookshelf Prefecture.

247
00:15:34,780 --> 00:15:36,320
A training camp, you say?

248
00:15:38,380 --> 00:15:39,460
Hey, Ryo-chan!

249
00:15:39,460 --> 00:15:41,740
Can we come over to your side too?

250
00:15:43,040 --> 00:15:43,680
Uh-oh.

251
00:15:43,680 --> 00:15:45,740
If these guys find out we're staying here,

252
00:15:45,740 --> 00:15:48,100
the lie that group guests
have to stay in the annex

253
00:15:48,100 --> 00:15:49,500
will be exposed!

254
00:15:50,400 --> 00:15:52,160
What, you're a group too?

255
00:15:53,620 --> 00:15:54,840
Come here for a second.

256
00:15:57,080 --> 00:15:58,020
Do what?

257
00:16:00,100 --> 00:16:02,060
What is that guy doing?

258
00:16:03,080 --> 00:16:03,800
Here, look.

259
00:16:03,800 --> 00:16:04,660
Let go!

260
00:16:06,700 --> 00:16:07,980
What do you think you're doing?

261
00:16:07,980 --> 00:16:10,340
You've warmed up enough by now, right?

262
00:16:10,340 --> 00:16:12,220
Get out of the bath already.

263
00:16:12,220 --> 00:16:14,680
"Get out"? What do you mean, "get out"?

264
00:16:14,680 --> 00:16:18,300
I'm only telling you this because I'm
worried about you getting called out.

265
00:16:18,300 --> 00:16:19,580
Mind your own business.

266
00:16:20,040 --> 00:16:21,940
Hondara Kenpō, Tsuma no Mae!

267
00:16:23,420 --> 00:16:26,260
You did it now, you perverted kappa!

268
00:16:29,520 --> 00:16:30,580
I can't forgive this anymore!

269
00:16:30,580 --> 00:16:31,660
Hondara Kenpō!

270
00:16:31,660 --> 00:16:32,740
Ear pull!

271
00:16:32,740 --> 00:16:36,220
Ow

272
00:17:07,820 --> 00:17:10,480
Right, as expected,
you came to peek at the bath, didn't you?

273
00:17:10,920 --> 00:17:12,980
N-no! This was an accident!

274
00:17:19,100 --> 00:17:21,240
Are Ryotsu and even the
Chief in on it together?

275
00:17:21,520 --> 00:17:23,920
N-no, that's a misunderstanding.

276
00:17:23,920 --> 00:17:24,520
Everyone!

277
00:17:25,740 --> 00:17:27,580
What is all this commotion?

278
00:17:27,580 --> 00:17:28,920
Well

279
00:17:28,920 --> 00:17:30,360
Where are the guests?

280
00:17:30,700 --> 00:17:31,740
S-sorry.

281
00:17:31,740 --> 00:17:34,640
We're staying in the annex, you know.

282
00:17:34,640 --> 00:17:35,960
Annex?

283
00:17:36,260 --> 00:17:38,880
We have no such thing at this hotel.

284
00:17:40,560 --> 00:17:41,340
Damn it!

285
00:17:41,340 --> 00:17:43,140
That clever bastard.

286
00:17:44,000 --> 00:17:45,980
Idiot!

287
00:17:50,860 --> 00:17:53,760
Using up the entire travel
budget on drinking money!

288
00:17:53,760 --> 00:17:55,840
I'm too appalled to even speak.

289
00:17:55,840 --> 00:17:58,720
Luckily,
the hotel says there are rooms available,

290
00:17:59,100 --> 00:18:00,740
so we'll stay there.

291
00:18:00,740 --> 00:18:05,180
They've even agreed to prepare their
famous octopus dish for us specially.

292
00:18:05,180 --> 00:18:09,360
But we'll deduct that cost
from your next paychecks.

293
00:18:10,020 --> 00:18:10,380
No way.

294
00:18:11,620 --> 00:18:14,460
You brought it on yourselves.
Reflect on it there.

295
00:18:16,540 --> 00:18:17,440
Damn it!

296
00:18:18,820 --> 00:18:19,920
Phew, thank goodness.

297
00:18:19,920 --> 00:18:21,520
I'm sorry, everyone.

298
00:18:22,500 --> 00:18:24,780
Jody, you don't need to worry about it.

299
00:18:24,780 --> 00:18:26,900
It's only those guys who are to blame.

300
00:18:27,360 --> 00:18:30,660
Jody, since you brought us all the way here,

301
00:18:30,660 --> 00:18:33,800
why don't you all come along to
the hotel and have dinner together?

302
00:18:33,800 --> 00:18:35,620
Oh-wa-da-ho!

303
00:18:47,660 --> 00:18:49,300
Well then, Chief, please.

304
00:18:49,300 --> 00:18:50,520
Thanks.

305
00:18:52,940 --> 00:18:55,320
And now, the hotel's famous

306
00:18:55,370 --> 00:18:57,800
all-octopus feast is ready for you to enjoy.

307
00:18:58,540 --> 00:19:01,300
Finally! I've been looking forward to this.

308
00:19:01,300 --> 00:19:03,540
Here it comes, the famous octopus dishes!

309
00:19:05,880 --> 00:19:10,200
I wonder if everyone's enjoying
delicious octopus dishes right now.

310
00:19:10,740 --> 00:19:12,880
It's just octopus.
You can eat that in Tokyo too.

311
00:19:12,880 --> 00:19:15,800
But this is top-grade octopus cuisine.

312
00:19:15,800 --> 00:19:18,300
I wish I could have at least tried a little.

313
00:19:18,300 --> 00:19:19,900
Octopus, naturally.

314
00:19:20,340 --> 00:19:21,740
I'm so hungry.

315
00:19:21,740 --> 00:19:23,320
Yeah, me too.

316
00:19:26,580 --> 00:19:27,260
Damn it!

317
00:19:27,260 --> 00:19:30,140
This is all the octopus's fault!

318
00:19:30,660 --> 00:19:32,560
Stupid octopus!

319
00:19:33,340 --> 00:19:34,580
Gah, I'm getting so pissed off!

320
00:19:34,580 --> 00:19:35,120
Ugh!

321
00:19:35,120 --> 00:19:35,860
Woah!

322
00:19:36,260 --> 00:19:36,960
S-Senpai!

323
00:19:36,960 --> 00:19:39,480
There was no need to kick it so hard...

324
00:19:39,480 --> 00:19:40,220
No way!

325
00:19:40,220 --> 00:19:42,300
How could a little kick
from me do that much...

326
00:19:46,560 --> 00:19:48,340
Whoa, what's going on?

327
00:19:48,600 --> 00:19:51,400
I-it looks like we're sinking!

328
00:19:51,400 --> 00:19:52,640
An accident?

329
00:19:52,840 --> 00:19:55,960
The outboard monitor showed it, right?
Here it is.

330
00:19:58,140 --> 00:20:01,160
First, we have fresh octopus sashimi.

331
00:20:01,940 --> 00:20:03,820
Ugh, how gross!

332
00:20:03,820 --> 00:20:07,120
T-this is an octopus!

333
00:20:07,460 --> 00:20:08,200
What?!

334
00:20:08,320 --> 00:20:12,260
An enormous octopus is
clinging to this ship!

335
00:20:29,900 --> 00:20:34,440
This is better than I expected, Ohara-kun.

336
00:20:34,440 --> 00:20:36,940
Next, we have octopus marinade.

337
00:20:38,120 --> 00:20:41,920
Wow, that looks delicious.
Thank you for the meal!

338
00:20:41,920 --> 00:20:45,760
Delicious! And so healthy, too!

339
00:20:51,700 --> 00:20:53,400
At this rate, we won't last.

340
00:20:54,280 --> 00:20:56,760
We're going to be eaten by the octopus.

341
00:20:56,760 --> 00:20:58,900
After all that octopus we've been eating...

342
00:20:59,720 --> 00:21:00,420
Don't cry!

343
00:21:02,820 --> 00:21:05,000
If it's come to this,
we have no choice but to move the boat!

344
00:21:05,180 --> 00:21:06,260
You can do it!

345
00:21:06,640 --> 00:21:08,340
I'm not the one steering!

346
00:21:08,920 --> 00:21:10,040
Then who?

347
00:21:10,360 --> 00:21:12,020
You! Come on!

348
00:21:12,420 --> 00:21:13,140
Wait, wait, wait!

349
00:21:13,720 --> 00:21:14,920
That's impossible!

350
00:21:15,320 --> 00:21:18,300
I've never even operated a submarine!

351
00:21:20,040 --> 00:21:21,500
It has a steering wheel!

352
00:21:21,660 --> 00:21:22,760
It's pretty much the same thing!

353
00:21:23,140 --> 00:21:24,920
You always make such unreasonable demands...

354
00:21:54,800 --> 00:21:58,220
It's delicious,
but it's like there are bones in it

355
00:22:01,080 --> 00:22:12,600


356
00:22:12,600 --> 00:22:14,120
It's really delicious!

357
00:22:14,120 --> 00:22:16,180
Good taste!

358
00:22:18,500 --> 00:22:20,180
I've reached my limit!

359
00:22:20,180 --> 00:22:21,620
Everyone's going to stop!

360
00:22:21,620 --> 00:22:41,680
And finally, the octopus dessert!

361
00:22:42,600 --> 00:22:44,740
It's rare for them to serve dessert, too.

362
00:22:53,200 --> 00:23:05,560
Ryotsu!

363
00:23:06,180 --> 00:23:08,560
Everyone, thank you,
now that the party is in full swing...

364
00:23:08,560 --> 00:23:10,860
What on earth is going on here!

365
00:23:12,600 --> 00:23:15,726
Just because they couldn't eat
the octopus dishes themselves,

366
00:23:15,776 --> 00:23:17,020
they pulled this kind of harassment!

367
00:23:17,280 --> 00:23:19,200
Nooo! W-wait, everyone!

368
00:23:19,460 --> 00:23:20,420
Lord Ryo!?

369
00:23:20,420 --> 00:23:21,560
I can't forgive this!

370
00:23:21,800 --> 00:23:23,040
What are you going to do about this!

371
00:23:23,320 --> 00:23:24,340
This is a complete mess!

372
00:23:25,040 --> 00:23:27,080
There's a deep reason behind this!

373
00:23:27,340 --> 00:23:30,060
We were attacked by a super giant octopus!

374
00:23:30,440 --> 00:23:33,360
If you're going to lie,
you'd better come up with a better lie!

375
00:23:33,480 --> 00:23:34,740
I-it's the truth, I swear!

376
00:23:34,740 --> 00:23:35,420
Bah-boo

377
00:23:35,740 --> 00:23:37,880
Aaaaaaah

378
00:23:37,880 --> 00:23:38,320
me

379
00:23:47,480 --> 00:23:48,360
Aaaaaaah

380
00:23:59,000 --> 00:24:02,120
I've had so much octopus,
I'm stuffed to the gills.

381
00:24:05,200 --> 00:24:06,620
Welcome, welcome!

382
00:24:07,680 --> 00:24:09,320
Welcome, welcome!

383
00:24:09,320 --> 00:24:11,360
Welcome, welcome, please come in!

384
00:24:12,440 --> 00:24:14,100
Welcome, welcome!

385
00:24:14,580 --> 00:24:16,120
Welcome, welcome, please come in!

386
00:24:17,340 --> 00:24:18,580
Welcome, welcome!

387
00:24:19,300 --> 00:24:20,680
Welcome, come right in!

388
00:24:21,780 --> 00:24:23,780
Um uh, well you see...

389
00:24:23,780 --> 00:24:25,260
Excuse me, may I ask something?

390
00:24:25,260 --> 00:24:26,180
Welcome!

391
00:24:26,180 --> 00:24:27,240
Then, anago roll.

392
00:24:27,240 --> 00:24:27,820
Janken roll.

393
00:24:27,820 --> 00:24:28,440
Salad roll.

394
00:24:28,440 --> 00:24:30,300
Anything rolls... what should I get?

395
00:24:31,040 --> 00:24:31,680
Right.

396
00:24:32,400 --> 00:24:34,260
Do you have California rolls?

397
00:24:34,620 --> 00:24:36,300
We don't have California rolls.

398
00:24:37,260 --> 00:24:38,900
This isn't America, you know.

399
00:24:39,640 --> 00:24:40,400
Sorry.

400
00:24:40,400 --> 00:24:44,440
Uh, excuse me.

401
00:24:58,960 --> 00:25:00,620
Was that a dad joke?

402
00:25:00,880 --> 00:25:02,280
Yes, sorry.

403
00:25:02,810 --> 00:25:04,760
I don't get it.

404
00:25:04,760 --> 00:25:07,240
Ah? Hm? Wait? Wait?

405
00:25:07,420 --> 00:25:08,360
Wait? Wait?

406
00:25:08,480 --> 00:25:09,160
Seriously?

407
00:25:09,340 --> 00:25:10,900
Welcome!

408
00:25:10,900 --> 00:25:13,100
Welcome, come in!

409
00:25:14,100 --> 00:25:15,800
Welcome!

410
00:25:15,800 --> 00:25:17,880
Welcome, come in!

411
00:25:17,880 --> 00:25:20,340
Welcome!

412
00:25:20,340 --> 00:25:21,980
Welcome!

413
00:25:21,980 --> 00:25:22,560
Welcome, please come in!

414
00:25:22,980 --> 00:25:25,280
Welcome!

415
00:25:25,280 --> 00:25:26,980
Welcome!

416
00:25:30,120 --> 00:25:34,900
Oh no, I just gave it a little
kick and the police box collapsed!

417
00:25:34,900 --> 00:25:39,660
Do I have to set up a temporary
police box until it's rebuilt?

418
00:25:39,660 --> 00:25:43,360
A convenient place like that doesn't just exist that easily,
you know.

419
00:25:43,360 --> 00:25:47,740
Next time, the temporary police box here.
See you!

420
00:25:48,660 --> 00:25:50,720
That place? It's Kame-ari!

421
00:25:51,960 --> 00:25:54,080
Well, I'm sure it's Kame-ari!

422
00:25:55,340 --> 00:25:59,280
Everyone, come on over to our town!

423
00:26:00,220 --> 00:26:00,920
Thank you.

